-- title:
--   Hecke correspondences on the uniformised fake-elliptic moduli curve
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N \neq 0$ and primes $q \neq q'$ with $q \nmid N$ and $q' \nmid N$, and a natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data.** For rationals $a,b$, the hypothesis `hB` asserts `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: either $a > 0$ or $b > 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Further data: a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of $B := \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order (an order — containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning and finitely generated — maximal among the orders containing it); $N$ squarefree; a submodule $R \le \Lambda$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R = \Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with $[\Lambda_1 : R] = N$; and an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota : B \to M_2(\mathbb{R})$. Throughout, $\mathrm{fuchsianGroup}\,R\,\iota$ denotes the intersection of the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $B^{\times}$ generated by the units of $R$ with the kernel of the determinant on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.
--
--   **Moduli data over $\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$.** An integral scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X : X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ (the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $D$), together with an assignment `pt` sending each commutative ring $S$, each morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} S \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ and each fake elliptic curve $E$ over $S$ (a relative abelian scheme whose fibres have dimension $2$, equipped with a commutative relative group law, a $\Lambda$-action by endomorphisms compatible with the group law and satisfying the trace condition $\operatorname{tr} = n$ whenever $m + \bar m = n$, and a level-$N$ structure `lev`) to a point of $X$ over $s$. The hypotheses on these data are: `hsmooth`, `hproper`, `hsmooth1` ($\pi_X$ smooth, proper, and smooth of relative dimension $1$); `pt_iso` (isomorphic fake elliptic curves over the same base give the same point, where `FakeEllipticCurve.Iso` means an isomorphism of the underlying schemes over the base respecting the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level structures); `pt_pullback` (for $\varphi : S \to S'$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $s$ equal to $s'$, and $E'$ a pullback of $E$ along $\varphi$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullback`, the point of $E'$ is the point of $E$ precomposed with $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$); `pt_surjective` and `pt_injective` (over an algebraically closed field $k$ every point of $X$ over $s$ is $\mathrm{pt}_k(E)$ for some $E$, and $\mathrm{pt}_k(E) = \mathrm{pt}_k(E')$ forces $E \cong E'$); and `hgeom` (all geometric fibres $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]} \operatorname{Spec} k$ are integral). Finally $\bar s$ is a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ with `sbar_over` saying that $\bar s$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}[1/D]$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   **The geometric generic fibre as a curve.** A field $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` which is a curve over it in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (every nonzero element has a degree-zero principal divisor, every place has residue field finite over the base, and $\Omega_{\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ is free of rank $1$) and essentially of finite type; a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{gal}$ from $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to the group of semilinear automorphisms of $\bar F$ (pairs of ring automorphisms of $\bar F$ and of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure map); a curve model $\mathfrak{M}$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an integral scheme $\mathfrak{M}.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with an identification of $\bar F$ with its function field and a bijection between closed points and places, compatible with stalks); and an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}} : \mathfrak{M}.C \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}[1/D]} \operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`he𝔐`) with $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ followed by the second projection equal to $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`he𝔐_snd`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a field $F_c$ with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure making it a curve over $\mathbb{C}$ and essentially of finite type, a uniformised Hecke curve structure $U$ for the group $\mathrm{fuchsianGroup}\,R\,\iota$ on $F_c$, a ring embedding $\mathrm{emb} : \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{toC} : \bar F \to F_c$ and a map $\mathrm{bcPlace}$ from places of $\bar F/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of $F_c/\mathbb{C}$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (i) The map $U.\mathrm{pt} : \mathbb{H} \to \mathrm{Place}\,\mathbb{C}\,F_c$ is surjective.
--
--   (ii) For every prime $\ell$ there is a finite set $S \subset B$ with: every $x \in S$ lies in $R$, has reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}\,x = \ell$, and satisfies $x \otimes 1 = h$ for some $h$ in `levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ` if $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet R ℓ` otherwise (the latter being the set of finite-idelic units $h$ lying in the adelic box of $R$ with $\ell h^{-1}$ in the box but $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}h$ not; the former cutting this down by the conditions that conjugation of $R$ by $h$ differs from $R$ and that $R$ is not contained in the conjugate of $\Lambda$ by $h$); every $y \in R$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,y = \ell$ admitting such a representative $h$ has a unique $x \in S$ with $y = ux$ for some unit $u$ of $R$ of reduced norm $1$; and the multiset $U.\mathrm{heckePoints}\,\ell$, pushed into $M_2(\mathbb{R})$, equals the image of $S$ under $\iota$.
--
--   (iii) For every $x \in F_c$ and $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$ the function $z \mapsto U.\mathrm{realize}\,x\,(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ is meromorphic at $\tau$.
--
--   (iv)–(vi) Near every $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$, in the punctured-neighbourhood filter, $U.\mathrm{realize}$ is additive, multiplicative, and sends $\mathbb{C}$-scalars to the corresponding constants.
--
--   (vii) If two elements of $F_c$ have realizations agreeing eventually near every $\tau$, they are equal.
--
--   (viii) Every realization is invariant under $\mathrm{fuchsianGroup}\,R\,\iota$, eventually near every $\tau$.
--
--   (ix) Every function $f : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ which is meromorphic at every point of $\mathbb{H}$ and invariant under $\mathrm{fuchsianGroup}\,R\,\iota$ in the above eventual sense is the realization of some element of $F_c$.
--
--   (x) $\mathrm{toC}$ is compatible with $\mathrm{emb}$: $\mathrm{toC}(\lambda \cdot 1) = \mathrm{emb}(\lambda) \cdot 1$ for $\lambda \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   (xi) The subfield of $F_c$ generated by $\mathbb{C}$ together with $\mathrm{toC}(\bar F)$ is all of $F_c$.
--
--   (xii) $\mathrm{toC}$ preserves linear independence: a finite subset of $\bar F$ independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has $\mathbb{C}$-independent image.
--
--   (xiii) For every place $P$ of $\bar F$ and every $x \in \bar F$, $\mathrm{toC}\,x$ lies in the valuation subring of $\mathrm{bcPlace}\,P$ if and only if $x$ lies in that of $P$.
--
--   (xiv) **Hecke correspondences in moduli terms.** For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $q$ and $q'$, every place $P$ of $\bar F$ and every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose moduli point $\mathrm{pt}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\bar s, E)$ equals the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $P$ by $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$, followed by $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ and the first projection to $X$, there exist $n \in \mathbb{N}$, extra levels $K_0,\dots,K_{n-1}$ at $\ell$ on $E$ (each an $\ell$-torsion, $\Lambda$-stable, finite flat subgroup scheme of rank $\ell^2$, closed under the group law and inverses, meeting the level structure of $E$ trivially, and geometrically isomorphic to $\mathbb{Z}/\ell \times \mathbb{Z}/\ell$), fake elliptic curves $d_0,\dots,d_{n-1}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and places $P_0,\dots,P_{n-1}$ of $\bar F$ such that: the $K_i$ are pairwise distinct as subfunctors of points (if $K_i$ and $K_j$ are factored through by the same points of $E$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ then $i = j$); every extra level at $\ell$ on $E$ has the same points as some $K_i$; for each $i$ the pair $(E, K_i)$ admits a level-$\ell$ isogeny onto $d_i$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsLevelIsogeny` (mutually dual morphisms $\varphi, \psi$ over the base, homomorphic for the group laws, commuting with the $\Lambda$-action, with $\varphi\psi$ and $\psi\varphi$ the action of $\ell$, with kernel of $\varphi$ exactly the points factoring through $K_i$, and with $\varphi$ carrying the level structure of $E$ into that of $d_i$); the moduli point of each $d_i$ is the point attached to $P_i$ in the same way; and
--   $$U.\mathrm{corr}\,\ell\,\big(\delta_{\mathrm{bcPlace}\,P}\big) = \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \delta_{\mathrm{bcPlace}\,P_i}$$
--   as divisors on $F_c/\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   (xv) **Atkin–Lehner at $q$ and at $q'$.** For all places $P, Q$ of $\bar F$ and all fake elliptic curves $E, E'$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose moduli points are the points attached to $P$ and to $Q$ respectively, if $E'$ is an Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $q$ in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient` (mutually dual morphisms between $E$ and $E'$, homomorphic for the group laws and commuting with the $\Lambda$-action, whose composites are the action of $q$, the kernel of $\varphi$ being the points killed by every $m \in \Lambda$ with $m\bar m$ a rational integer multiple of $q$, and $\varphi$ carrying level structures to level structures), then $U.\mathrm{corr}\,q\,(\delta_{\mathrm{bcPlace}\,P}) = \delta_{\mathrm{bcPlace}\,Q}$; and the same statement with $q'$ in place of $q$.
--
--   This is the complex-uniformisation step for the Shimura curve attached to an Eichler order $R$ of squarefree level $N$ in an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ and $q'$: the geometric generic fibre of the coarse moduli scheme of fake elliptic curves is matched with a quotient of the upper half-plane by the Fuchsian group of $R$, in such a way that the $\ell$-th Hecke correspondence of the analytic model is computed on points by the sum over extra levels at $\ell$ (equivalently, $\ell$-isogenies), and the correspondences at $q$ and $q'$ by the Atkin–Lehner involutions. It is stated with no reference to a moduli tower, and is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_bcPlace_corr_eq_correspondence_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.exists_uniformizedHeckeCurve_bcPlace_corr_eq_correspondence_of_two_mul_dvd), where the dictionary is transported to the push–pull correspondences of a tower.
